{
  "case_id": "2009-08-6261",
  "document_hash": "e25f15dd25d6f23945887dda358dcac24a8632ecf7a22dce8ce4d08742f73946",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Jaclyn S. Frankfurt, Esq., on behalf of the Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2009-08-6261",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e25f15dd25d6f23945887dda358dcac24a8632ecf7a22dce8ce4d08742f73946",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e25f15dd25d6-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. FRANKFURT: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: This case presents the question whether, under our Constitution, the power to prosecute criminal contempt in a Federal court rests solely with the sovereign. The United States now agrees that the fact that a criminal offense may only be prosecuted by the sovereign is a foundational premise of our Constitution. Because Mr. Robertson was prosecuted for criminal contempt in a private right of action, his prosecution was unconstitutional, a nullity in our view, and his convictions must be vacated."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-08-6261",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e25f15dd25d6f23945887dda358dcac24a8632ecf7a22dce8ce4d08742f73946",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e25f15dd25d6-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Excuse me. We have plenty of plea agreements jurisprudence that say if the Southern District of New York prosecutes someone and they sign a plea agreement and say, we're not going to prosecute you for further crimes, we read that to mean that the Southern District of New York won't prosecute you for further crimes. We don't read it that no other government agency is bound, who has jurisdiction over that criminal activity, that they are equally bound."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-08-6261",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e25f15dd25d6f23945887dda358dcac24a8632ecf7a22dce8ce4d08742f73946",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e25f15dd25d6-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 16,
        "start": 16
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Does -- does the Justice Department concede that the sovereign here is the United States?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice STEVENS",
      "case_id": "2009-08-6261",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "e25f15dd25d6f23945887dda358dcac24a8632ecf7a22dce8ce4d08742f73946",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e25f15dd25d6-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So, no, the question would be whether the lawyer for the -- the party who entered into the settlement could bring a contempt proceeding against the adversary who had violated the settlement."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. FRANKFURT",
      "case_id": "2009-08-6261",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "e25f15dd25d6f23945887dda358dcac24a8632ecf7a22dce8ce4d08742f73946",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e25f15dd25d6-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think the strongest case is Gompers v. Buck's Stove. That says fundamentally -\u00ad and I'm not quoting verbatim -- but it says fundamentally erroneous as if a tort action of A -- for battery of A versus B, a sentence of 12 months is imposed."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. FRANKFURT",
      "case_id": "2009-08-6261",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "e25f15dd25d6f23945887dda358dcac24a8632ecf7a22dce8ce4d08742f73946",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e25f15dd25d6-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Court should go with the Third and Fourth Circuits who have -- expressed -- quite eloquently about the United States not being a bunch of separate fiefdoms, but that when the United States speaks, they speak for the government at large."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Robert A. LONG",
      "case_id": "2009-08-6261",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "e25f15dd25d6f23945887dda358dcac24a8632ecf7a22dce8ce4d08742f73946",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e25f15dd25d6-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think it's very important to be clear about what is properly before the Court. This started out as a case about a plea agreement, and the Petitioner's claim is that his plea agreement with the U.S. Attorney barred his criminal contempt proceeding."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice SOTOMAYOR",
      "case_id": "2009-08-6261",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "e25f15dd25d6f23945887dda358dcac24a8632ecf7a22dce8ce4d08742f73946",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e25f15dd25d6-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I -- I'm not sure I understand your point. Yes, the caption doesn't have to be styled in a particular name -\u00ad"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice SOTOMAYOR",
      "case_id": "2009-08-6261",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "e25f15dd25d6f23945887dda358dcac24a8632ecf7a22dce8ce4d08742f73946",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e25f15dd25d6-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is the real party in interest the United States?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice BREYER",
      "case_id": "2009-08-6261",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "e25f15dd25d6f23945887dda358dcac24a8632ecf7a22dce8ce4d08742f73946",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e25f15dd25d6-0001-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I would like to know whether the government could appoint the private person."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-08-6261",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e25f15dd25d6f23945887dda358dcac24a8632ecf7a22dce8ce4d08742f73946",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e25f15dd25d6-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you think that Congress could -- could set up a private organization to expend Federal funds -- we are going to abolish the Department of Education. And we are going to give its function to a private organization that will take care of all those things. No good, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-08-6261",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e25f15dd25d6f23945887dda358dcac24a8632ecf7a22dce8ce4d08742f73946",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e25f15dd25d6-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I'm not sure why -- how we can avoid it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Kagan",
      "case_id": "2009-08-6261",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e25f15dd25d6f23945887dda358dcac24a8632ecf7a22dce8ce4d08742f73946",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e25f15dd25d6-0002-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There are two questions, properly raised, in this case. Petitioner is right about one. Respondent is right about the other and the disposition."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2009-08-6261",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e25f15dd25d6f23945887dda358dcac24a8632ecf7a22dce8ce4d08742f73946",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e25f15dd25d6-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: But do I understand your position that in this particular case the U.S. Attorney could have entered into a settlement agreement that would have bound the Respondent?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Kagan",
      "case_id": "2009-08-6261",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e25f15dd25d6f23945887dda358dcac24a8632ecf7a22dce8ce4d08742f73946",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e25f15dd25d6-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL KAGAN: We actually don't think that that's right, Justice Stevens. We think that in fact the U.S. Attorney did not bind the Respondent, but we don't think it could have bound the Respondent, and it"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-08-6261",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e25f15dd25d6f23945887dda358dcac24a8632ecf7a22dce8ce4d08742f73946",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e25f15dd25d6-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: I don't know that courts have ever asserted that they themselves have the power to prosecute."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2009-08-6261",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e25f15dd25d6f23945887dda358dcac24a8632ecf7a22dce8ce4d08742f73946",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e25f15dd25d6-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 61,
        "start": 61
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Well, if there were a finding of innocent, or not guilty, by this prosecutor, could the official prosecutor then prosecute again, or would there be double jeopardy? If you are saying they are somehow separate, does the double jeopardy clause apply?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2009-08-6261",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e25f15dd25d6f23945887dda358dcac24a8632ecf7a22dce8ce4d08742f73946",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e25f15dd25d6-0003-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 63,
        "start": 63
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Counsel, could I ask you could a 1983 or I guess Bivens action be brought against Ms. Watson?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2009-08-6261",
      "confidence": 0.0,
